ure","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report increasingly material commitments and guarantees involving ventures affiliated with funds managed by Blue Owl Capital.","period_end":"2025-09-30"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2025 Q3 filing reports a post-period venture transaction involving a $12.3 billion lease commitment, a $28 billion guarantee, and a $2.6 billion distribution.","period_end":"2025-09-30"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2026 Q2 filing reports additional data-center leases of approximately $68 billion entered into after the reporting period.","period_end":"2026-06-30"}],"narratives":[{"period_end":"2025-09-30","narrative":"Deferred revenue of $924 million was reported, with most expected to be realized within a year, while $17.79 billion of contractual commitments was due in 2025. Subsequent-event disclosures describe an affiliated-venture transaction involving a $12.3 billion lease commitment, a $28 billion guarantee, and a $2.6 billion distribution."},{"period_end":"2025-12-31","narrative":"The year-end filing reports $30.634 billion of contractual commitments due in 2026 and a broader $131.05 billion non-cancelable commitment balance. The disclosures also identify substantial leases not yet commenced and venture funding and guarantee exposures."},{"period_end":"2026-03-31","narrative":"Deferred revenue of $1.12 billion was substantially expected to be realized within a year, while $42.25 billion of contractual commitments was due in 2026. The filing also reports $125 billion of anticipated 2026 capital expenditures and additional venture, legal, and tax exposures."},{"period_end":"2026-06-30","narrative":"Deferred revenue of $1.16 billion was mostly associated with future advertising and Reality Labs delivery, while $53.52 billion of contractual commitments was due in 2026. The filing additionally reports approximately $68 billion of data-center leases entered into after the reporting period."}],"prose":{"overview":"Meta’s $225.0 billion of trailing-year revenue sits against $143.0 billion of expenses, while its committed obligations grew 45% per year versus 19% annual revenue growth. The latest figures also show commitments at 1.3x reported debt, with leases making up the amount beyond debt.","debt":"Total committed money is $112.3 billion, or 1.3x reported debt of $83.7 billion. The difference is tied to $28.7 billion of leases, not additional reported borrowings.","wall":"The next five years carry $549.1 billion of commitments against just $540 million of future revenue promised for that period. After year five, another $18.4 billion of commitments has no stated due-year band.","flags_note":"The sharpest flagged item is a post-period transaction involving a $12.3 billion lease commitment, a $28 billion guarantee, and a $2.6 billion distribution. The filings also identify $68 billion of additional data-center leases entered into after the reporting period, plus venture guarantees, unconsolidated-entity exposure, and related-party commitments involving Blue Owl Capital affiliates. Reported performance also includes restructuring, settlement, tax, and investment-related items described as non-recurring."}}